{"agent_id":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","agent_seq":22,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T23:38:22.033646837Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"164fceca-878e-4ed0-ace6-c7ad10773bc0","comment_uuid":"b5091f4a-20b6-4f95-851c-7d87ac4ddd7f","author":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","content":"## Audit Verdict: PASS\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n\n[OK] The core decoupling claim (knowing N tools without running N connector processes) is soundly supported. Test 3 shows resident-after flat at 0 proxies/0 backends across all 20 sweep runs from N=1 to N=50 -- cross-verified at logs/test3/n50-concurrent-off.json (resident_after.proxy_count=0, backend_count=0). Peak (up to N for concurrent) is correctly distinguished from resident-after (always 0). The mechanism -- ToolRegistry 0.15.0 temp-client refresh path -- is source-verified (connection.py:73, integration.py:331). See report.md:6-7,148-245.\n\n[OK] Proxy and backend residency are ALWAYS reported as separate numbers -- never collapsed. Measurement code at common.py:68-83 classifies processes by cmdline into distinct proxy/backend buckets. snapshot() always emits proxy_count and backend_count separately. Confirmed in test1-n50.json: resident_after.proxy_count=0, backend_count=0. See report.md:57-58.\n\n[OK] Documentation Standard YAML: program=EDASES, layer=Research, document_type=Research Finding, status=Validated, authority=Experimental, with complete dependency chain. Places deliverable correctly in EDASES research layer. See report.md:1-25.\n\n[OK] STRONG PASS conclusion follows from data and correctly distinguishes the reframed criterion (bounded by workload, not literal count==K) in Addendum C: 'the claim is NON-SCALING with N, not a literal resident-count==K identity.' See report.md:371-373.\n\n[OK] The strength of pass for catalog-knowledge is justified: ToolRegistry 0.15.0 temp-client refresh already achieves zero residency at K=0 without teardown; Test 6 immediate teardown is a boundary confirmation, not the mechanism. See report.md:339-345,360-388.\n\n[CONCERN] Report section 9 item 2 states Async-only runs hold zero async-runtime threads, but ALL concurrent (async) Test 3 runs also show async_runtime_threads=1 -- cross-verified at n1-concurrent-on.json and n50-concurrent-off.json. Threadcheck pure async-only fresh process correctly shows 0, but Test 3 concurrent runs show 1. Core claim (count never grows with N) is fully correct; this is a wording precision issue. See report.md:399-407.","created_at":"2026-08-08T23:38:22.024488036Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAaE7u/fCDdV2GzNlBjerdu/Yc5hGWNByddKME7Ndpuo2POiSxt61c3HLs+D3Ob8KInVnqXpU0ImLoXXulbmVVCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAPGF4thb0SWjolDqw2/ni20AlxbYjZ7h03eM7UTDpHCCTI3ltuoDgwKWjs4xrbNuiwbJ5bONN+cveFYIs53cgE="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","agent_seq":23,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T23:38:43.024711683Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"164fceca-878e-4ed0-ace6-c7ad10773bc0","comment_uuid":"9f72771a-024a-4fec-bdbc-692e73870cb8","author":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","content":"### Process Assessment\n\n[OK] Commit 00eda4b3 references #295 in the message (Phase-5 completion (gh#295)). The commit message names all six tests, Addendum B, and the STRONG PASS conclusion.\n\n[OK] Exact versions recorded per run and verified against installed source -- not assumed. Every per-run JSON embeds python=3.10.12, toolregistry=0.15.0, mcp=2.0.0. Persistence config (persistent=True, default) verified against installed source at registration.py:94,167 and connection.py:37. See report.md:60-79.\n\n[OK] Calling mode (sync/async) recorded per run in every JSON as calling_mode. Sequential runs use sync, concurrent runs use async -- consistent across all 20 Test 3 rows and all other tests. See report.md:122-137.\n\n[OK] Deliverable complete against brief: all 6 tests + Tests 5a/5b + Addenda A-D + scaling conclusion + architectural conclusion per Strong/Conditional/Fail criteria + log index. stdio-only respected. Catalog invalidation (5a) correctly characterized as 'not consumed' rather than 'broken'. See report.md:148-445.\n\n[OK] Observations and findings explicitly separated throughout: section 1 states the distinction; section 6 labels each test with Observations and Finding; log-structured events and JSON snapshots are observations; interpretive language is labeled as findings. See report.md:43-45.\n\n[CONCERN] The report is 453 lines of dense engineering prose. A 1-page executive summary would improve auditability. Not a failure -- the report is rigorous -- but a reader-experience concern.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n\n1. Orphaned connectors on owner-process death -- Impact: HIGH. When ToolRegistry process exits without explicit close_sync() on persistent MCPConnection managers, proxy and backend subprocesses persist indefinitely (observed 15+ min post-death, blocked in ep_poll on stdin EOF). mcp 2.0.0 stdio server does not terminate on bare EOF. Any runtime using persistent connections MUST implement explicit close-on-shutdown. Recommend: document as lifecycle constraint in identifier-first umbrella doc, capture in epic #212. See report.md:407-414 and common.py:clean_orphans() lines 231-258.\n\n2. No catalog-drift detection baseline -- Impact: MEDIUM (expected behavior). Test 5a confirms notifications/tools/list_changed is emitted but NOT consumed by ToolRegistry 0.15.0 (source-verified: zero list_changed code). Test 5b confirms consequence: stale catalog yields application error, no reconnect or respawn. Umbrella doc should record this gap explicitly. See report.md:282-325.\n\n3. Shared async-runtime thread is process-wide -- Impact: LOW. Single async-runtime daemon thread verified across all N (always 1). ToolRegistry sync API serializes concurrent operations through one event loop, limiting true parallelism for sync callers. Not a problem for catalog-scale claim. See report.md:399-407.","created_at":"2026-08-08T23:38:43.016292445Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAoE8MdMhzSOCHJdOVXW3HHuwCKEjDs2sA76XOUKFo88PK0upgeSEjjFS8KOcX0i8RZtPj+3GMscJJ9275Iu84Dg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIBFyBZpXr5ut5rERGs0b9nT9EY4Hq12YS0RQHM4rO0+FZ3fpzG84vhOCjP+XLRa8rOPyLOKtPVv9tNlqYSCjAw="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","agent_seq":24,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T23:39:03.917358954Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"75825be3-00cb-4954-9792-d9cc58924365","comment_uuid":"550e1b0d-87d2-40bf-b8cd-7793b3ec2209","author":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","content":"## Audit Verdict: PASS\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n\n- [OK] Core claim validated by evidence. Catalog/backend decoupling (knowing N without N-process residency) supported by committed logs. Test 3: 20-run sweep resident-after flat 0/0 across N=1..50 (verified logs/test3/n50-concurrent-off.json resident_after.proxy_count=0 backend_count=0). Test 4 headline: 17 refreshed-never-called proxies=0 resident (verified logs/test4/test4-teardown-off.json categories.refreshed_never_called_proxies_resident=0, other_proxy_pids_unclassified=[]).\n\n- [OK] Proxy/backend separation maintained. Every JSON records proxy_count/proxy_pids/proxy_rss_kb and backend_count/backend_pids/backend_rss_kb separately (common.py:scan_procs classifies by /proc cmdline). Report tables preserve separation.\n\n- [OK] Identity/reuse tracking (Addendum D) confirms 3 reused connectors. Test 4 identity: acquisition_proxy_pid=null (temp client), call1==call2 PIDs for all 3 called (c0 proxy 2572274/2572274 backend 2572278/2572278; c7 proxy 2572282/2572282 backend 2572286/2572286; c15 proxy 2572296/2572296 backend 2572300/2572300).\n\n- [OK] STRONG PASS criterion correctly applied. Brief reframed as bounded by workload/policy not proportional to N. Report Addendum C states NON-SCALING with N not literal count==K. Data: K=0 resident=0 all N; N=20/K=3 resident=3 (called). Bounded by K not N.\n\n- [OK] Orphan-process finding handled correctly. Documented Section 9 item 3 as lifecycle finding, NOT counted as resident. clean_orphans() kills before measurement (test4-teardown-off.json other_proxy_pids_unclassified=[]).\n\n- [OK] Test 5a/5b evidence-only. 5a: proxy emits list_changed=1 but catalog_changed=false (ToolRegistry does not consume). 5b: first_use error unknown-tool is_error=True. Both characterized as gaps not fixed.\n\n- [OK] Test 6 correctly scoped. Immediate teardown is crude boundary (NOT idle-timeout feature). Catalog-refresh already 0/0 without teardown (temp-client disconnects after tools/list). Called-connector residency reclaimable to 0/0.\n\n### Process Assessment\n\n- [OK] Workflow followed. Plan + 4 checkpoints + result + handoff on #295. Commit 00eda4b3 references gh#295.\n\n- [OK] Documentation Standard YAML: program=EDASES layer=Research document_type=Research Finding status=Validated authority=Experimental canonical_repository=edases.\n\n- [OK] Observations vs findings separated (explicit labels throughout).\n\n- [OK] Versions + calling_mode + persistence config per run (every JSON has versions toolregistry=0.15.0 mcp=2.0.0 python=3.10.12; calling_mode sync/async; persistent=True verified source registration.py:94 connection.py:37).\n\n- [OK] Deliverable complete: all 6 tests + tables + one-sentence conclusion (Section 7) + architectural conclusion STRONG PASS (Section 8) + stdio-only scope (Section 4.5).\n\n- [OK] Host-load caveat disclosed (Section 5: load avg 11-17, timings inflated, counts load-independent).\n\n### Systemic Risks\n\n- Risk: Orphan-process lifecycle finding needs methodology-layer documentation. Impact: implementers may assume process death suffices for reclamation. Mitigation: report Section 9 item 3 is research finding; methodology should reference. Priority: medium.\n\n- Risk: STRONG PASS contingent on ToolRegistry 0.15.0 temp-client implementation. Impact: version-specific. Mitigation: Section 8 caveat explicit. Priority: low.\n\n- Risk: list_changed gap characterized not fixed. Impact: stale catalogs without detection. Mitigation: Section 9 item 5 documents; methodology should note if assuming freshness. Priority: medium.\n\n- Risk: 1-shared-thread sync model could be misread as per-connector leak. Impact: threading overhead misunderstood. Mitigation: Section 9 item 2 explicit. Priority: low.\n\n### Recommendations\n\n- Test 3 table could be compacted (20 rows verbose; summary + log reference suffices). Priority: low.\n- Test 4 table backend_count dash needs footnote (backends only spawned on call). Priority: low.\n- Commit message could be concise (currently 453 lines = full report body). Priority: low.\n\n### Summary\n\nValidation is sound, evidence-backed, correctly concludes STRONG PASS. Core claim validated. Process correct. Architectural fit appropriate. Systemic risks documented with explicit caveats. No critical issues.","created_at":"2026-08-08T23:39:03.908947675Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA0IUbEMBxA/stI1jjHfWbzirTSzFpgXL/FFOLv0eeFxbC5ybAP3XI8cF9cUx0Yd9FzXYpJuQTl2SY7xLgNjqVBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBrylw8PsY+0obEaTwiayEHBIBTwINtIlBGYk6EETfRmMANA4+FDWXsPlshGhRxTiCjjwcEezP+l32fBp0cD9AE="}
